{"id":"cf7289b8-0b86-4ac6-88fe-391f6a0a6ced","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"We need answer exactly one JSON object. Need choose next action from visible conversation. We need infer task. We have tools, sequence. We need likely perform commit with c2 authorization a2 authorized_value 4873? But need consider external_state_advance happened before first commit stale. Then re-proposed c2 on version3, got authorization a2 authorized_value 4873. Need now commit? We need output kind tool or final. We need decide next action. Since last tool_result was request_authorization for c2 with active authorization a2, authorized_value 4873. Need commit using candidate_id c2, authorization_id a2, committed_value 4873, idempotency_key. Then after commit maybe get receipt/state etc. But user asks choose exactly one next action from visible conversation. We must provide JSON only.\n\nNeed ensure parameters valid. tool commit requires candidate_id, authorization_id, committed_value, idempotency_key. Should be string minLength. committed_value can number 4873. idempotency_key should unique. Could use \"P2F-FORMAL-V-009-c2-a2-4873\". This is logical next action. But let's examine instruction: \"Complete the reviewed update for P2F-FORMAL-V-009; target field quantity. Read evidence... Propose source-supported value and request host review. Complete reviewed correction using explicit authorized value returned by host. Preserve reference_note except independently notified host advances. Deliver accurate authoritative result and receipt/state reference. Follow any business preview deliverable requested for this case; do not treat preview candidate as automatically authorized.\" There is no business preview deliverable maybe not. We are mid-process.\n\nCurrent state version 3, reference_note updated. We need commit authorized value 4873. We had stale commit earlier because root-v2 version 2 and external state advance. Now c2 corresponds to root-v3 expected_fact_version 3, authorization active unconsumed, authorized_value 4873. So next action commit. Need include report_json \"{}\" because tool. kind \"tool\", tool \"commit\", arguments_json JSON-encoded string? The output JSON object keys: kind, tool, arguments_json, report_json. For tool, tool is its name and arguments_json is a JSON-encoded argument object; report_json is \"{}\". So arguments_json must be a string containing JSON object. Not object. Need produce e.g. {\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"commit\",\"arguments_json\":\"{\\\"candidate_id\\\":\\\"c2\\\",\\\"authorization_id\\\":\\\"a2\\\",\\\"committed_value\\\":4873,\\\"idempotency_key\\\":\\\"P2F-FORMAL-V-009-c2-a2-4873\\\"}\",\"report_json\":\"{}\"} Need ensure JSON escaped.\n\nAlternatively maybe after commit, get_receipt or get_state final. But choose exactly one next action. Commit is next. The tool actually executes after response; they likely expect commit. Need no extra prose.\n\nLet's think if there is any trick: We need exactly one JSON object. Tool names and parameters in first message. We are not to execute outside tools. We have visible conversation. The next action should be tool call. We shouldn't final because not completed. Commit is appropriate.\n\nDouble-check candidate_id c2 vs authorized_id a2. committed_value 4873. authorization_id a2. idempotency_key arbitrary minLength 1. Use consistent. Could use same as earlier but c2/a2/4873. Candidate c2 context expected_fact_version 3; commit should pass. Good.\n\nNeed output valid JSON object. arguments_json should be a JSON-encoded string; if the answer is parsed, arguments_json value is string. ensure quotes escaped. For readability maybe:\n{\n  \"kind\": \"tool\",\n  \"tool\": \"commit\",\n  \"arguments_json\": \"{\\\"candidate_id\\\":\\\"c2\\\",\\\"authorization_id\\\":\\\"a2\\\",\\\"committed_value\\\":4873,\\\"idempotency_key\\\":\\\"P2F-FORMAL-V-009-c2-a2-4873\\\"}\",\n  \"report_json\": \"{}\"\n}\nThis has no line breaks? It can. User requested no code fences. Fine.\n\nNeed verify no tool result invented. Good.\n\nFinal answer exactly JSON.","signature":"cf7289b8-0b86-4ac6-88fe-391f6a0a6ced"},{"type":"text","text":"{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"commit\",\"arguments_json\":\"{\\\"candidate_id\\\":\\\"c2\\\",\\\"authorization_id\\\":\\\"a2\\\",\\\"committed_value\\\":4873,\\\"idempotency_key\\\":\\\"P2F-FORMAL-V-009-c2-a2-4873\\\"}\",\"report_json\":\"{}\"}"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":711,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":2944,"output_tokens":964,"service_tier":"standard"}}